  "goodToKnow": "Die Fasnacht (also Fastnacht) is Carnival in south-west Germany and Switzerland, the night before Lent (die Fastenzeit). The Swabian-Alemannic Fasnacht features Narren in carved wooden masks, as in Rottweil, while Basler Fasnacht, on UNESCO's intangible heritage list, starts with the Morgestraich at 4 a.m. Elsewhere it's Fasching (Bavaria, Austria) or Karneval (Rhineland). It has no plural."
